From 175ef6feb555bbf67bcdfff7f628d686decf63a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 13:31:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: consider gloves as armour-swap candidates

borg_notice_armour_swap()'s wearable switch covered rings, amulets,
boots, helms, crowns, shields, cloaks and the three body-armour tvals
but not TV_GLOVES, so gloves of Free Action or combat egos were never
candidates for the armour swap. Add case TV_GLOVES:. Class-sensitive
glove concerns (caster mana penalties) are already handled by the
main-gear glove logic; the swap is only worn situationally. Owner
intent recorded on the issue 2026-11-07.
---
 src/borg/borg-trait-swap.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-trait-swap.c b/src/borg/borg-trait-swap.c
index 084248062..81e8c909a 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-trait-swap.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-trait-swap.c
@@ -850,6 +850,7 @@ void borg_notice_armour_swap(void)
         case TV_HELM:
         case TV_CROWN:
         case TV_SHIELD:
+        case TV_GLOVES:
         case TV_CLOAK:
         case TV_SOFT_ARMOR:
         case TV_HARD_ARMOR:
-- 
